# Line endings, settled once rather than per checkout.
#
# Git on Windows converts LF to CRLF by default. Left alone that means every
# file looks modified the moment the repo is cloned on the Surface, every diff
# is noise, and anything that cares about its own bytes — a shell script, a
# snapshot, an ffmpeg concat list written by a test — behaves differently on
# one machine than the other.
#
# So: normalised in the repository, LF in the working tree everywhere. Windows
# tooling has handled LF for years; the conversion is the thing causing trouble.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, and must never be touched by any of the above. A CRLF conversion
# inside a PNG is not a diff, it is a corrupt file.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mov binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.m4a binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.onnx binary
*.bin binary
*.cube binary
